6. Remote Identity & Repository Provenance Findings (Gate 0.4B §5.1)
Local vs. Remote Root Lineage Split (CRITICAL — G01, G02): verify_remote_identity() checks rev-list --max-parents=0 HEAD exclusively in the local repository (L239) and only checks that refs/heads/$EXPECTED_PROD_BRANCH exists on origin (L248). When EXPECTED_PROD_HEAD_SHA is unset (its default), pointing origin to an unrelated bare repository (G01) or a force-pushed orphan main branch (G02) passed AUDIT_HISTORY_PASS (rc=0).
Remote Branch Creation Race (CRITICAL — G03): cmd_push() omits --force-with-lease="refs/heads/$RECOVERY_BRANCH:" (expecting empty/absent ref). When an unexpected backup/stage-1b.2-verified branch appeared on origin pointing to main after stage, cmd_push silently fast-forward overwrote it (ce0d8b7..14a0aae). Existing tags (G04) and divergent branches (G05) were safely rejected atomically.
Repository Object Format (INFO / Policy Gap): require_hex40() (L60, L206, L208) enforces 40-character lowercase SHA-1 hashes. SHA-256 Git repositories (extensions.objectFormat=sha256, 64-char hashes) are implicitly rejected without documenting this restriction or checking git rev-parse --show-object-format.
