12. Bash Reliability & Error-Handling Findings (Gate 0.4B §5.6)
Broken trap ... RETURN Breaks Transactional Quarantine & Cleanup (CRITICAL — G21, G23, G25):
Lines 491 (cmd_prepare_export), 593 (cmd_stage), and 779 (cmd_restore_test) register RETURN traps.
In Bash, calling exit 1 inside die() triggers EXIT, NOT RETURN.
Proven in G21: Triggering die() mid-cmd_stage left g21_stage unquarantined (quarantined=0, unquarantined_left=YES).
Proven in G23: Triggering die() inside cmd_restore_test leaked /tmp/pdfsun-restore-test.* (restore_tmp_leaked=1).
Proven in G25: Line 590 also masks quarantine mv failures with 2>/dev/null || true and uses 1-second date -u +%s collision-prone names.
Hidden git rm Failure (MEDIUM — L612): git -C "$STAGE_CLONE_DIR" rm -rf --ignore-unmatch . >/dev/null 2>&1 || true masks genuine index-lock or permission errors.
No Concurrency Lock (MEDIUM — G24): Zero flock usage (flock_refs=0); simultaneous invocations race on STAGE_CLONE_DIR (p1_rc=1, p2_rc=0).
Leaked mktemp Files (LOW — L360–361, L623–624): Temporary comparison files leak on die() prior to rm -f.
Container Root Caveat (G22): Read-only directory test chmod 500 succeeded (rc=0) because this sandbox runs as uid=0 (root), where discretionary 0500 modes do not block writes; non-root write-failure testing requires an unprivileged user on the Owner workstation.
